    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0405" n="331" xml:id="pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister of Supply</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Beaverbrook</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Hopkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-28">December 28,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Harry</hi>, I enclose a copy of a letter and
                    document which I have sent to the President this morning.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d189-f1"/> I have also sent a copy to the Prime Minister and attach
                    a copy of my Minute to him.</p>
                <p>If the leaders of our race will look at the supply situation they will see the
                    imperative necessity for an immense increase in production here and in Great
                    Britain. Canada may also be relied upon to do something more.</p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Max</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d189-a1.xml" xpointer="d189-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
